  "user_request_original": "Design a planar multilayer dielectric filter for 1550 nm LiDAR receiver. Incident medium is Air. Substrate is Fused Silica. Use exactly 29 layers with materials Ta2O5 (Gao) and SiO2 (Lemarchand). Stack structure: Air | (Ta2O5 (Gao)/SiO2 (Lemarchand))_7 | Ta2O5 (Gao) | (SiO2 (Lemarchand)/Ta2O5 (Gao))_7 | Fused Silica. Optimize all 29 layer thicknesses to maximize transmittance at 1550 nm while minimizing transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Wavelength bands for evaluation: 1400-1500 nm (suppression), 1550 nm (transmission peak), 1600-1700 nm (suppression). Normal incidence assumed. Total layer count fixed at 29. Materials: Ta2O5 (Gao) (high index), SiO2 (Lemarchand) (low index).",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design a 29-layer planar dielectric filter on fused-silica using alternating Ta2O5 and SiO2 coatings to maximize transmission at 1550 nm while minimizing transmission in the 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Optimize all 29 layer thicknesses at normal incidence.",
